{"chunk_id": "64a09910f0f6", "text": "Yudhishthira notices Krishna sitting in deep meditation and wonders at the cosmic stillness of his yogic state. When Krishna returns to ordinary awareness, he explains that his mind had been fixed upon Bhishma, who lies dying on a bed of arrows and is contemplating him. Krishna praises Bhishma\u2019s unmatched prowess, learning, and moral wisdom, warning that when Bhishma departs the world, vast knowledge will vanish with him. He urges Yudhishthira to approach the grandsire and question him about kingship, duty, morality, and the paths of life before his passing. As the sun begins its northern course, sages gather around the dying hero. Bhishma, radiant despite his wounds, fixes his mind on Krishna and offers an immense hymn praising him as the supreme cosmic being\u2014source, sustainer, and dissolution of the universe\u2014expressed through countless divine forms.\nKrishna meditates on the dying Bhishma, urging Yudhishthira to learn from him before his passing, as Bhishma on his arrow-bed praises Krishna as the Supreme.\nThemes: divine devotion, approaching death, supreme divinity of Krishna, transmission of wisdom, yogic concentration", "vector": [0.006391899660229683, -0.005166101269423962, 0.010476800613105297, 0.0056327590718865395, -0.010365065187215805, 0.02757882885634899, -0.030023854225873947, -0.012586620636284351, -0.01524854265153408, -0.01200165506452322, 0.014959346503019333, -0.0005804469692520797, 0.0018633456202223897, 0.005770784802734852, -0.012836380861699581, -0.0025978391058743, 0.050083573907613754, 0.008458997122943401, 0.04306398704648018, -0.02606712095439434, -0.005323844496160746, -0.011035475879907608, 0.0014435177436098456, 0.012514321133494377, -0.021597720682621002, 0.026448333635926247, 0.018942371010780334, -0.02128223329782486, -0.014433533884584904, -0.028393838554620743, -0.0064379083923995495, 0.006102703511714935, -0.0030891443602740765, -0.005593323148787022, -0.02318830043077469, 0.0018